+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant, `qty` a whole
+  number). Each dish sold uses one portion of its recipe per `qty`; the
+  ingredients are consumed with ledger `ref` `sale:<ticket>` at `soldAt`.
+  Tickets already imported are skipped. Answers `{ "tickets", "dishes" }`
+  (new tickets, and dishes sold on them). If a row is invalid
+  (`bad_request`) or an item runs out (`sale_not_enough_stock`), nothing is
+  imported and the message names the row (`row 2` is the first data row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists
+  `{ itemId, theoretical, actual, difference }` per item: theoretical use
+  from sales sold in those days (inclusive), actual use from every `consume`
+  movement in those days, `difference = actual - theoretical`. Items where
+  both are zero are left out.
+
